Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:44:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/25] Plugins: JSON from a listed web service (a2.web.get,
 web:<host>)

A plugin's page has no network at all, and some data plugins want is
only on the web: a market plugin needs the market prices players collect
on aion2.exchange (its public API; it sends no CORS headers, so a page
couldn't read it anyway). await a2.web.get(url) now returns the parsed
JSON answer of a service the meter lists (plugins::WEB_HOSTS:
aion2.exchange, and on raw.githubusercontent.com only the Clicktrough
fork's branch market-data, its hourly copy of those prices), for a
plugin with the permission "web:<host>"
(Settings words it "Read data from <host> on the internet"): GET over
https only, no other host, path, port or credentials, at most 8 MB, null for
a 404. One address is read at most once a minute, whichever plugin
window asks, and one host at most four times a second.

A failed request says why, as the player can act on it: "could not
connect: ... Connection refused", "no answer in time", "the service is
down right now (it answered 503 ...)", not only reqwest's "error sending
request for url (...)". A connection that failed is tried once more over
IPv4 alone (an IPv6 path that leads nowhere, or drops the large packets
of a long certificate chain, while the browser on HTTP/3 never notices;
once that helped, IPv4 first for the session), and a 502, 503 or 504
once more after two seconds.

